    || setweight(to_tsvector('english', 'Difficulty: Easy · LeetCode 110
Problem
Given a binary tree, determine if it is height-balanced (left and right subtree heights differ by at most 1 for every node).
Understanding the problem
A tree is balanced if abs(height(left) - height(right)) <= 1 for all nodes.
Intuition
Return -1 immediately when an unbalanced subtree is found.
Approach
Define dfs(node): if node is None return 0.
left = dfs(node.left); if left == -1 return -1.
right = dfs(node.right); if right == -1 return -1.
If abs(left - right) > 1 return -1.
Return 1 + max(left, right).
Naive Solution
Repeatedly calculate subtree heights.
class Solution:
    def isBalanced(self, root):

        def height(node):
            if not node:
                return 0

            return 1 + max(
                height(node.left),
                height(node.right)
            )

        if not root:
            return True

        left = height(root.left)
        right = height(root.right)

        if abs(left - right) > 1:
            return False

        return (
            self.isBalanced(root.left) and
            self.isBalanced(root.right)
        )
