SELECT '55457dc6-ca62-771e-b8d4-263eea823056', 'cc774680-bd67-74c3-bda5-3499586c52f7', 'Single Number', 'Single Number', 'Difficulty: Easy · LeetCode 136
Problem
Every number in the array appears exactly twice except one. Find that single number. You must solve it in O(n) time and O(1) space.
Understanding the problem
XOR has two golden properties: x ^ x = 0 (pairs cancel) and x ^ 0 = x (identity). XOR-ing all elements causes every duplicate pair to vanish, leaving only the unique number.
Intuition
XOR all elements together. Paired numbers cancel to 0. The single unpaired number XOR''d with 0 returns itself.
Approach
Initialize answer = 0.
For each num in nums: answer ^= num.
Return answer.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Use a hash set: add unseen numbers, remove them when seen a second time. Whatever remains is the answer.
class Solution:
    def singleNumber(self, nums):
        seen = set()

        for num in nums:
            if num in seen:
                seen.remove(num)
            else:
                seen.add(num)

        return seen.pop()
class Solution {
public:
    int singleNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        unordered_set<int> seen;

        for (int num : nums) {
            if (seen.count(num)) {
                seen.erase(num);
            } else {
                seen.insert(num);
            }
        }

        return *seen.begin();
    }
};
class Solution {
    public int singleNumber(int[] nums) {
        Set<Integer> seen = new HashSet<>();

        for (int num : nums) {
            if (seen.contains(num)) {
                seen.remove(num);
            } else {
                seen.add(num);
            }
        }

        return seen.iterator().next();
    }
}
var singleNumber = function(nums) {
    const seen = new Set();

    for (const num of nums) {
        if (seen.has(num)) {
            seen.delete(num);
        } else {
            seen.add(num);
        }
    }

    return seen.values().next().value;
};
Time: O(n) · Space: O(n)
Optimized Code (Python 3)
