INSERT INTO "notes"."NoteSearchDocument" ("noteId", "versionId", "title", "topics", "body", "document", "updatedAt")
SELECT 'a928a651-7e68-703a-bf9a-17e86fa80312', '1416ac34-1314-743e-83e8-9727bc74eb80', 'Reorder List', 'Reorder List', 'Difficulty: Medium · LeetCode 143
Problem
Reorder list to follow: L0 → Ln → L1 → Ln-1 → L2 → ...
Understanding the problem
Interleave first half with reversed second half.
Intuition
Three steps in O(1) space: 1. Find middle (Fast/Slow) -> 2. Reverse second half -> 3. Interleave merge.
Approach
Find middle: slow and fast pointers.
Reverse second half starting at slow.next, split list.
Interleave merge two lists first and second.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Store node references in array, set left/right pointers to re-link.
class Solution:
    def reorderList(self, head):
        nodes = []

        current = head

        while current:
            nodes.append(current)
