Problem
Given intervals and queries, for each query return the size of the smallest interval that contains it, or -1 if none exists.
Understanding the problem
Sorting both intervals and queries lets us add intervals incrementally as queries grow. A min-heap ordered by interval size keeps the best candidate at the top. Expired intervals (those ending before the current query) are lazily removed.
Intuition
Sort intervals by start and queries (with original indices) by value. Sweep queries left-to-right: push all intervals whose start ≤ query onto a min-heap keyed by size. Pop intervals from the heap whose end < query (expired). The heap top is the smallest valid interval.
Approach
Sort intervals by start.
Create sorted_queries = sorted((q, i) for i, q in enumerate(queries)).
Initialize result = [-1] * len(queries), heap = [], i = 0.
For each (query, original_index): push all intervals with start <= query as (size, end).
Pop heap entries where end < query (expired intervals).
If heap is non-empty: result[original_index] = heap[0][0].
Return result.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
For every query, scan all intervals linearly and find the smallest containing one.
class Solution:
    def minInterval(self, intervals, queries):
        result = []

        for query in queries:
            best = float("inf")

            for start, end in intervals:
                if start <= query <= end:
                    size = end - start + 1
                    best = min(best, size)

            result.append(-1 if best == float("inf") else best)

        return result
class Solution {
public:
    vector<int> minInterval(vector<vector<int>>& intervals, vector<int>& queries) {
        vector<int> result;

        for (int query : queries) {
            int best = INT_MAX;

            for (auto& interval : intervals) {
                int start = interval[0], end = interval[1];

                if (start <= query && query <= end) {
                    int size = end - start + 1;
                    best = min(best, size);
                }
            }

            result.push_back(best == INT_MAX ? -1 : best);
        }

        return result;
    }
};
class Solution {
    public int[] minInterval(int[][] intervals, int[] queries) {
        int[] result = new int[queries.length];

        for (int q = 0; q < queries.length; q++) {
            int query = queries[q];
            int best = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

            for (int[] interval : intervals) {
                int start = interval[0], end = interval[1];

                if (start <= query && query <= end) {
                    int size = end - start + 1;
                    best = Math.min(best, size);
                }
            }

            result[q] = best == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? -1 : best;
        }

        return result;
    }
}
var minInterval = function(intervals, queries) {
    const result = [];

    for (const query of queries) {
        let best = Infinity;

        for (const [start, end] of intervals) {
            if (start <= query && query <= end) {
                const size = end - start + 1;
                best = Math.min(best, size);
            }
        }

        result.push(best === Infinity ? -1 : best);
    }

    return result;
};
