SELECT '1abd0ed4-bbce-719a-baf7-f739dbc3eee6', 'e9ca97a6-318d-7418-b7f9-737d735d033f', 'Design Add and Search Words Data Structure', 'Design Add and Search Words Data Structure', 'Difficulty: Medium · LeetCode 211
Problem
Design a data structure supporting addWord(word) and search(word) where ''.'' in search patterns matches any single character.
Understanding the problem
A wildcard ''.'' means branching into every child of the current Trie node simultaneously — a DFS over all children.
Intuition
Build a Trie for fast prefix traversal. When encountering ''.'', branch into all children via DFS and return True if any branch succeeds.
Approach
Build Trie with TrieNode(children, is_word) exactly as LC 208.
addWord inserts into the Trie identically.
search(word) calls dfs(index, node).
Base case: index == len(word) → return node.is_word.
If word[index] != ''.'': advance into node.children[char] if exists.
If word[index] == ''.'': iterate all node.children.values() and return True if any recursive call returns True.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Store words in a list and compare each candidate against the search pattern character-by-character.
class WordDictionary:

    def __init__(self):
        self.words = []

    def addWord(self, word):
        self.words.append(word)

    def search(self, word):

        for candidate in self.words:

            if len(candidate) != len(word):
                continue

            match = True

            for i in range(len(word)):

                if (
                    word[i] != "."
                    and word[i] != candidate[i]
                ):
                    match = False
                    break

            if match:
                return True

        return False
class WordDictionary {
public:
    WordDictionary() {}

    void addWord(string word) {
        words.push_back(word);
    }

    bool search(string word) {
        for (const string& candidate : words) {
            if (candidate.size() != word.size()) continue;

            bool match = true;

            for (int i = 0; i < (int)word.size(); i++) {
                if (word[i] != ''.'' && word[i] != candidate[i]) {
                    match = false;
                    break;
                }
            }

            if (match) return true;
        }

        return false;
    }

private:
    vector<string> words;
};
