SELECT '74583a21-6c57-7594-b996-0e8fa55331e4', '08286ac2-8be3-76ed-bcde-66f84dececa2', 'Missing Number', 'Missing Number', 'Difficulty: Easy · LeetCode 268
Problem
Given an array containing n distinct numbers from [0, n], return the one missing number.
Understanding the problem
XOR the complete range 0..n with every element of the array. Present numbers cancel in pairs; only the missing number has no partner to cancel with.
Intuition
Start with answer = n. For each index i, XOR in both i and nums[i]. Every index 0..n-1 is covered, and each present number cancels. The missing number survives.
Approach
Initialize answer = n.
For i, num in enumerate(nums): answer ^= i, answer ^= num.
Return answer.
Naive Solution — Brute Force
Put all numbers in a set; scan 0..n for the missing one.
class Solution:
    def missingNumber(self, nums):
        n = len(nums)
        values = set(nums)

        for num in range(n + 1):
            if num not in values:
                return num

        return -1
class Solution {
public:
    int missingNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        unordered_set<int> values(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        for (int num = 0; num <= n; num++) {
            if (!values.count(num)) {
                return num;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        Set<Integer> values = new HashSet<>();
        for (int num : nums) {
            values.add(num);
        }

        for (int num = 0; num <= n; num++) {
            if (!values.contains(num)) {
                return num;
            }
        }

        return -1;
    }
}
var missingNumber = function(nums) {
    const n = nums.length;
    const values = new Set(nums);

    for (let num = 0; num <= n; num++) {
        if (!values.has(num)) {
            return num;
        }
    }

    return -1;
};
Time: O(n) · Space: O(n)
Optimized Code (Python 3)
class Solution:
    def missingNumber(self, nums):
        n = len(nums)
        answer = n

        for i, num in enumerate(nums):
            answer ^= i
            answer ^= num

        return answer
class Solution {
public:
    int missingNumber(vector<int>& nums) {
        int n = nums.size();
        int answer = n;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            answer ^= i;
            answer ^= nums[i];
        }

        return answer;
    }
};
class Solution {
    public int missingNumber(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int answer = n;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            answer ^= i;
            answer ^= nums[i];
        }

        return answer;
    }
}
var missingNumber = function(nums) {
    const n = nums.length;
    let answer = n;

    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        answer ^= i;
        answer ^= nums[i];
    }

    return answer;
};
Time: O(n) · Space: O(1)
Takeaway
Pattern — Missing value in known range → XOR complete range with array (also solvable as sum(0..n) - sum(nums))',
