  ('a7fbf7be-5f2e-79fe-bfb0-63b2e936bd24', 'aI', 'code', '{"language":"cpp","code":"class Solution {\npublic:\n    string alienOrder(vector<string>& words) {\n        unordered_map<char, unordered_set<char>> graph;\n        for (auto& word : words)\n            for (char c : word) graph[c];\n\n        for (int i = 0; i + 1 < (int)words.size(); i++) {\n            const string& w1 = words[i];\n            const string& w2 = words[i + 1];\n            int minLength = min(w1.size(), w2.size());\n\n            if (w1.size() > w2.size() && w1.compare(0, minLength, w2, 0, minLength) == 0)\n                return \"\";\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < minLength; j++) {\n                if (w1[j] != w2[j]) {\n                    graph[w1[j]].insert(w2[j]);\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        // true = on the current path (cycle), false = finished\n        unordered_map<char, bool> visited;\n        string result;\n\n        function<bool(char)> dfs = [&](char c) -> bool {\n            if (visited.count(c)) return visited[c];\n\n            visited[c] = true;\n\n            for (char neighbor : graph[c])\n                if (dfs(neighbor)) return true;\n\n            visited[c] = false;\n            result += c;\n\n            return false;\n        };\n\n        for (auto& [c, _] : graph)\n            if (dfs(c)) return \"\";\n\n        reverse(result.begin(), result.end());\n        return result;\n    }\n};","filename":"C++"}'),
  ('f415a785-1402-7a1d-af38-2e972e4fd421', 'aJ', 'code', '{"language":"java","code":"class Solution {\n    private Map<Character, Set<Character>> graph = new LinkedHashMap<>();\n    // true = on the current path (cycle), false = finished\n    private Map<Character, Boolean> visited = new HashMap<>();\n    private StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();\n\n    public String alienOrder(String[] words) {\n        for (String word : words)\n            for (char c : word.toCharArray())\n                graph.putIfAbsent(c, new HashSet<>());\n\n        for (int i = 0; i + 1 < words.length; i++) {\n            String w1 = words[i], w2 = words[i + 1];\n            int minLength = Math.min(w1.length(), w2.length());\n\n            if (w1.length() > w2.length() && w1.startsWith(w2))\n                return \"\";\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < minLength; j++) {\n                if (w1.charAt(j) != w2.charAt(j)) {\n                    graph.get(w1.charAt(j)).add(w2.charAt(j));\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        for (char c : graph.keySet())\n            if (dfs(c)) return \"\";\n\n        return result.reverse().toString();\n    }\n\n    private boolean dfs(char c) {\n        if (visited.containsKey(c)) return visited.get(c);\n\n        visited.put(c, true);\n\n        for (char neighbor : graph.get(c))\n            if (dfs(neighbor)) return true;\n\n        visited.put(c, false);\n        result.append(c);\n\n        return false;\n    }\n}","filename":"Java"}'),
  ('0cc61cec-3632-72b6-bb13-b91422cfd6d1', 'aK', 'code', '{"language":"javascript","code":"var alienOrder = function(words) {\n    const graph = new Map();\n    for (const word of words)\n        for (const c of word)\n            if (!graph.has(c)) graph.set(c, new Set());\n\n    for (let i = 0; i + 1 < words.length; i++) {\n        const w1 = words[i], w2 = words[i + 1];\n        const minLength = Math.min(w1.length, w2.length);\n\n        if (w1.length > w2.length && w1.startsWith(w2)) return \"\";\n\n        for (let j = 0; j < minLength; j++) {\n            if (w1[j] !== w2[j]) {\n                graph.get(w1[j]).add(w2[j]);\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // true = on the current path (cycle), false = finished\n    const visited = new Map();\n    const result = [];\n\n    const dfs = (c) => {\n        if (visited.has(c)) return visited.get(c);\n\n        visited.set(c, true);\n\n        for (const neighbor of graph.get(c))\n            if (dfs(neighbor)) return true;\n\n        visited.set(c, false);\n        result.push(c);\n\n        return false;\n    };\n\n    for (const c of graph.keys())\n        if (dfs(c)) return \"\";\n\n    return result.reverse().join(\"\");\n};","filename":"JavaScript"}'),
